hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17742","Waki narrated to us, Dawud al-Zaafiri narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Khanbash al-Tai who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umra in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"17743","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Dawud al-Awdi narrated to us, from Amir, from Harim ibn Khanbash who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, in which of the months shall I perform Umra. He said: Perform Umra in Ramadan, for an Umra in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"17744","Abdullah narrated to us, my father and Yahya ibn Main narrated to me, both saying: Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and once Waki said: And Sufyan said: from Bayan and Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Wahb ibn Khanbash al-Tai who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umra in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
